    <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>Shared bus</header>
      <memberdef kind="define" id="group__x430__config_1ga9113a25601c31edb2986778731fdc703" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>X430_TURN_TIMEOUT_MS</name>
        <initializer>(100U)</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Longest wait, in milliseconds, for the status packet of the device before a hosted device in a SYNC_READ or BULK_READ (default 100). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>On a bus shared with devices of other buses (other MCUs, real servos), a hosted device answers a SYNC_READ or BULK_READ only after it has received the status packet of the ID listed just before it, like an X series actuator. When that status does not arrive within this time after the last progress of the read, the remaining hosted devices of the read stay silent. A new instruction packet ends the wait as well. The time comes from the millisecond clock of <ref refid="structx430__port" kindref="compound">x430_port</ref>; without a clock the wait ends only with the next instruction packet. Keep it longer than one status packet at the lowest baud rate in use, plus the Return Delay Time. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/x430_config.h" line="122" column="10" bodyfile="inc/x430_config.h" bodystart="122" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
